From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] libbinder: a host binder context (Waydroid's dual driver) for device HALs

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md, docs/HALIUM.md). A second binder context, /dev/host_binder (apklayer's path layer maps it to
$APKLAYER_HOST_BINDER: a Halium device's own /dev/binder, or another instance's binder in the two-instance test), beside the
instance's own: ProcessState::self(true) and IPCThreadState::self(true) (own TLS key, own thread pool), BpBinder remembers
its context, Parcels received through it (by buffer address) or carrying its proxies use it, buffers are freed through it.
BackendUnifiedServiceManager falls back to the host's servicemanager for names listed in /data/apklayer/host_hals.conf
(written per instance from the provider choice) and reports them declared. Ported from Waydroid's frameworks/native 0015
(Android 13) to Android 16, with two additions for older hosts (Halium 9-13): the host lookup uses getService (transaction 1
since Android 11; checkService moved in 14), and binder stability travels as a Category (version | level << 24): read in
either form, and written so (null binders too) once a host reply showed it. Not ported: 0009 (host uid as system uid; for
host processes calling into ours).
ABI kept: the Parcel flag sits in KernelFields padding (64-bit only: 32-bit has none and knows received parcels only), new functions are overloads. Rebuild: `m libbinder`.
Against frameworks/native 46018f54b424 (REVISION), after 0001-0005. Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
